<!-- Root cause: the code layout in flow mode. The code panel is shaped like an editor window — the three
     dots and the file path in the title bar say "this is real code". The panel takes the full slide width
     and the remaining height with `grow="1"`, and below it a three-step cause → effect chain is joined by
     connectors.

     `lang="go"` is in the vocabulary, so the code is pasted **verbatim from gofmt** — indentation is tabs
     (the theme's `code.tabSize` expands them to 2), and highlighting is built by the value layer from the
     token stream.

     Only the last link of the chain has an `accent5` border — it is what the incident cost (the deck's
     color rule — 001_cover). -->
<slide id="root-cause" layout="code" enter="rise">
  <text variant="kicker">Root cause</text>
  <h2>Every expiry landed at the same moment</h2>
  <shape type="rounded-rect" variant="card" fill="surface" border="none" w="fill" grow="1" pad="0">
    <col gap="0" h="fill">
      <shape type="rect" fill="alpha(fg, 0.06)" border="none" w="fill" pad="xs md">
        <row gap="xs" align="center">
          <shape type="ellipse" fill="accent5" border="none" w="12" h="12"/>
          <shape type="ellipse" fill="accent4" border="none" w="12" h="12"/>
          <shape type="ellipse" fill="accent3" border="none" w="12" h="12"/>
          <text role="code" size="15" color="muted">  payments/cache/warm.go — called by the deploy hook</text>
        </row>
      </shape>
      <col gap="0" pad="sm lg" grow="1" justify="center">
        <pre lang="go" size="19">// Fill the cache in one pass on deploy — every TTL ends up at the same instant.
func warm(ctx context.Context, ids []string) error {
	for _, id := range ids {
		if err := cache.Set(ctx, key(id), load(id), 30*time.Minute); err != nil {
			return err
		}
	}
	return nil
}</pre>
      </col>
    </col>
  </shape>
  <row gap="2xl">
    <shape type="rounded-rect" id="c1" fill="none" border="1 solid muted" radius="md" grow="1" basis="0" pad="sm md">
      <col gap="0"><text role="heading" size="22">① Bulk warm-up</text><text role="caption">120k keys filled in seconds</text></col>
    </shape>
    <shape type="rounded-rect" id="c2" fill="none" border="1 solid muted" radius="md" grow="1" basis="0" pad="sm md">
      <col gap="0"><text role="heading" size="22">② Fixed 30-min TTL</text><text role="caption">No jitter, so expiries converge</text></col>
    </shape>
    <shape type="rounded-rect" id="c3" fill="alpha(accent5, 0.12)" border="2 solid accent5" radius="md" grow="1" basis="0" pad="sm md">
      <col gap="0"><text role="heading" size="22" color="accent5">③ All miss at once</text><text role="caption">Each miss becomes a DB query</text></col>
    </shape>
  </row>
  <connector from="c1" to="c2" enter="draw"/>
  <connector from="c2" to="c3" variant="accent" line="2 solid accent5" enter="draw"/>
  <note>Fixed TTL plus bulk warm-up equals a stampede. We had neither jitter nor single-flight.</note>
</slide>
